{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/72846-the-darkest-grimest-thing-you-done-on-owod","id":72846,"title":"The darkest/grimest thing you done on OWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T15:25:45-08:00","id":72846,"title":"The darkest/grimest thing you done on OWoD","content":"its called world of darkness for a reason :/ , sometimes some dms cross the lines, or use things that are incredibly grim and unsettling.... what have you done?<br /> <br /> on my wraith game i had a character who was killed at a columbine esque massacre, the twist.. He is the killer, and his shadows manifests as his own guilt and the wraiths of those who he killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:59:32-08:00","id":72858,"title":"","content":"My darkest chronicle ever was a Wraith game, hands down.<br /> <br /> Most of the characters in it were regular people on the surface with terrible secrets that were often buried in their subconscious minds a-la Silent Hill, such as a character who discovered that he was the responsible for the death of her teenage girlfriend, now turned a spectre, when he pushed her to have an illegal abortion years before his own demise. At the end of the chronicle, all but one player decided his character would walk right into the Maelstrom to be torn apart into Oblivion, as they deserved it from their sins.<br /> <br /> Funny thing is, though most of the players enjoyed the game, they wouldn't ever play Wraith again, as it was too grimdark for their taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":355,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","user":"romanov","date":". 02-15-2014, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:23:42-08:00","id":73064,"title":"","content":"Led my players in the solemn enactment of a satanic ritual. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, this is a Hunter game, and as a group of PC's we had spent the last 3 games chasing down a brutal cult, and gathering clues that they quickly discovered were elements of a ritual that the cult was going to perform. One of the PC's was blackmailed, and he gave up all of the things that the group had gathered to the cult. And over the course of those games, they had created a pretty wordy and intricate ritual. All the details, and occult symbology, and the spooky words and all. They were a bunch of philosophy/theology geeks who love to chew scenery, so you can imagine how far they ran with it.<br /> <br /> The next game, I switched it up on them, and had each of them play a member of the cult. I took the role of the high priest. They already knew the ritual. So, we busted out the black robes(I had 6 of them, matching, made for a con long ago. We were Sith.) and we did exactly what our parents always feared we would do one day, and summoned Satan in the livingroom. I -was- planning to have them switch back to their PC's before the ritual could be completed, but they all decided that they didn't want to change back until it was over, and they could drink the kool-aid I had made for them.<br /> <br /> So, the ritual went off without a hitch, and the next game the regular PC's found the mass suicide that the ritual had left behind, and ominous hints that the End could not be stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T07:50:57-08:00","id":73185,"title":"","content":"I hurt someone's feelings once.<br /> <br /> Okay, serious answer - hunted down a mortal murderer because he was a threat to the Masquerade (and being Humanity 7 I also didn't like murderers...) beat him to death and left him in a shallow grave. Not much closure for the victims' families...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T15:14:01-08:00","id":73409,"title":"","content":"Right....he hunted down and murdered someone because he didn't like murderers ? How did your character deal with the inherent hipochrisy of that ?<br /> <br /> My darkest things are always from the adversary POV, since I tend to ST. As a player, I suppose embracing a child &quot;prodigy&quot; (she probably would have been a powerful mage if she'd been allowed to grow up) as a malkavian just to see if I could preserve her powers of foresight forever ranks up there.<br /> <br /> Of course, it backfired on my poor Malkavian in the most terrible way, but that's what you get, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","user":"HOD","date":". 02-16-2014, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T17:37:04-08:00","id":73468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/72846-the-darkest-grimest-thing-you-done-on-owod?p=73409#post73409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right....he hunted down and murdered someone because he didn't like murderers ? How did your character deal with the inherent hipochrisy of that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not well, let's just say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T19:33:52-08:00","id":75390,"title":"","content":"Based on several decisions and one epically bad roll, i lead my troupe into a scenario where they ended up sending the Stargazers into &quot;Extinct in the Wild&quot; status. Basically there were less then 20 in the entire world when it was said and done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:26:21-08:00","id":75913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/72846-the-darkest-grimest-thing-you-done-on-owod?p=75390#post75390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on several decisions and one epically bad roll, i lead my troupe into a scenario where they ended up sending the Stargazers into &quot;Extinct in the Wild&quot; status. Basically there were less then 20 in the entire world when it was said and done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that is harsh. How did that happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:24:33-08:00","id":76040,"title":"","content":"The game started before revised edition, so when it came out and said the main caern was going to fall and the gazers were going to basically go to the beast courts they wanted to be involved in that and there pack thought it would be awesome. So I did a couple of scenes that lead to them being there during the time of the fall. Basically Chimera gave one of them a vision of something bad going to happen and they went on a quest to warn them. The pack was made up of 2 stargazers, an Uktena, a Glasswalker, and a Silverfang. To make a long story short the Silverfang thought it would be a great idea to have the glasswalker set up explosives in the escape canyon so that if they needed to retreat they could blow the path on the way out and protect the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> Everyone agreed, the fight happened, they stayed in the battle to long trying to rack up as much renown as they could until the Stargazers called it quits.As they are running out glasswalker goes to trip the first set of explosives with control simple machine and botches hardcore (by hardcore, i mean on 7 dice he gets 4 1's and no successes). Ends up setting off all of the charges. 75% of the tribe is buried in the canyon with the BSD. The ones that ran into Umbra were slaughtered by Wyrm minions on the other end. At the time the only packs outside of the caern were an envoy to the Beast Courts and the Nation asking for aid and a few stragglers who hadn't made it home yet.<br /> <br /> Up until this point they had never failed a mission, the dice loved them. This was an epic failure that changed the whole direction of the pack. The rest of the chronicle was them trying to save as many of the Stargazers left in the world as they could and get them to the Beast Courts safely. There would about 15 stragglers + the 2 envoys which were about 5 wolves each so 25 NPC Stargazers left in the world at that point. 1 pack didn't make it, ended up dying saving the PCs.<br /> <br /> Throughout this the Glasswalker and Silverfang ended up losing their shit. Glasswalker started giving in more and more to the weaver. More upgrades to make him better so he could redeem himself. The silverfang fell the other way, he and the Uktena ended up dabbling with banes. He lost his mind and nearly got the pack killed because of the whisper of a chance at more power (this is what cost them the other 5 gazers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 02-20-2014, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:41:41-08:00","id":76045,"title":"","content":"I developed a vampire elder, 5th Gen, who was seeking to free vampires from preying on humans. To effect this, he opened a night only medical clinic next to the police department. He then used blood bonds on the local detectives to arrange for the occasional disappearance of &quot;undesirables&quot; and other untraceable persons. As an ancient student of thaumaturgy, he then experimented on these persons to combine them with succulents, like aloe, to create plants that would directly photosynthesize human blood. As all the experiments had to be done on living specimens, and many attempts were utterly unsuccessful, this might qualify as a vehicle speeding along that road paved with good intentions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":".  A more perfect sentence. 02-20-2014, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:52:37-08:00","id":76052,"title":"","content":"I was running a Vampire the Masquerade game that I named &quot;Broken Choices&quot; none of the players ever caught on to the fact that the name of the chronicle was also the theme. So: <br /> <br /> When they felt they could get away with Diablerie because they were attacking a Sabbat City, rather then spending their time trying to infiltrate or track down members for assassination, the Coterie leader, (a Malkavian who was built like an Assamite who basicly had Megalomania) felt that the best solutions would always involve pipe bombs and the kind of explosives that flattened buildings. <br /> <br /> After they successfully brought the city of Portland to it's knees in an assumed terrorist attack that had successfully destroyed a large number of key infrastructures they decided to go after the sabbat leaders! Long story short: they attacked the Harbingers of the skulls and successfully diablerized two of them. In a feeding frenzy and diablerie-off one of our newest players succeeded, and there was a huge difference between the two generations so he was very happy to get his extra blood expenditures but wondered why he didn't get some kind of cool discipline, I told him that it didn't make sense to just learn some diciplines out of the blue so that his powers would have to develop.<br /> <br /> When they returned to their home city he decided to feed from a woman he picked up at a bar and get a little nookie in the process. He accidentally Thanatosis'd the woman as I asked him for a willpower roll and oh my did he botch. The look of horror as the player realized not only did his character kill his date but that she had become a mummified corpse wraped around his body in flagrante delicto was priceless. It took him three more games of accidentally activating his bonus dots of Thanatosis before he got full control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T20:48:51-08:00","id":76080,"title":"","content":"The second worst thing ive done in oWoD is had one of the characters ghouls beaten to a pulp and disfigured with a knife(almost skined her face) and the other ghoul was also killed but at least it was quick<br /> <br /> the worst thing involves a baseball bat and the same antagonist as above","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T05:02:17-08:00","id":76191,"title":"","content":"When I was in college, I once played a Red Talon Philodox who successfully sterilized hundreds of homid Garou (mostly Glass Walkers), over a thousand human kin and something like 85% of the populations of Montreal, Toronto, Vancouver and Edmonton. Including one of his own pack mates (though that was inadvertant). . During an infiltration of a Magadon facility in New Jersey (Wyrm-tainted Pentex corporation's pharmaceutical arm, for those not familiar with Werewolf), my character got separated from the pack. While on his own, he found an R&amp;D lab where they were working on spiritually active bioweapons. He tortured the researcher who was present to find out what everything did, then took the one that interested him- a strain that was virtually undetectable and caused irreversible sterility in humans and homid Garou. Magadon considered it a failure they were trying to only target the Garou and couldn't make the virus selective enough. He destroyed the rest, then secretly started introducing it to the water supply at select caerns and in the aforementioned cities. The pack was nomadic and ended up spending a lot of time in Canada because of a quest we were doing for the Wendigo (I forget the details), and he figured using it in Canadian cities would be more effective than using it in the US since it would take less effort to depopulate Canada. The punchline-he got away with it! Suspicion was deflected onto Magadon and Pentex, and when they finally realized that it had to be a Garou accessing these caerns, the Wendigo pack member got blamed because none of the stuff had ever been released in any Wendigo caern or First Nations population. After the Wendigo pack member was killed for it, my character stopped using it and passed his remaining supply to some Red Talon elders to decide what to do with it (he only had enough left for maybe two more cities at that point anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T05:06:54-08:00","id":76193,"title":"","content":"Man, that's some dark stuff! Can I be friends with you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T09:48:16-08:00","id":76351,"title":"","content":"I played this DA:M game years ago where after Mistridge and some other clashes between the Craftmasons and the Order of Hermes brought the two Fellowships to the brink of war between them. But there were members of both trying prevent this. That's where we came in. Our cabal consisted of two Craftmasons (myself and another) and two members of the OoH working together to broker a peace before things spiral out of control.<br /> <br /> Long story short, our cabal traveled across Europe, negotiating with various leaders among both groups, carrying little quests to appease some, prevented an assassination attempt on one and removed another. All the while the ST was selling us on the idea that depending on our actions we could change history, perhaps even preventing the rise of the Order of Reason and the Traditions leading to a whole different future. Ultimately we were successful, our masters coming together at the Tower of Languedoc (currently a Heremtic chantry) in France to iron out an accord. First night there a big glorious feast and everything seemed to be going so well, a happy conclusion to a long but excellent chronicle.<br /> <br /> But it was... well it was the Red Wedding* with the Heremtics blindsiding the Masons and those Heremtics that sought peace.<br /> <br /> Worse it was started by the Heremtic players who privately approached the ST early on about this and help craft this whole betrayal. Virtually the entire time we were going about trying to bring together the two Fellowships they were plotting our downfall. Needless to say we were pissed off when the reveal happened and the killing began.<br /> <br /> Of course some of the Masons did manage to escape (us included) and in the Epilogue, set a decade later, we got our revenge on them, destroying a major Heremtic chantry in the process.<br /> <br /> *If Game of Thrones the TV series existed back then I suspect that the ST would have played The Rains of Castamere just before the big reveal, just to have that &quot;Oh shit...&quot; moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:23:29-08:00","id":76757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>romanov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/72846-the-darkest-grimest-thing-you-done-on-owod?p=76193#post76193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that's some dark stuff! Can I be friends with you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. Nothing like attempted genocide to make friends. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:24:26-08:00","id":77314,"title":"","content":"Wow, this stuff all seems really light by comparison to my games. Granted I run a lot of Sabbat, but still...<br /> <br /> <b>WARNING: THE BELOW STORY IS COMPLETELY NSFW! SKIP OVER THIS IF YOU DO NOT WANT TO READ REALLY SICK STUFF.</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ok. I think the darkest thing I've seen (I was the ST in this game) involved a Malkavian antitribu pedophile with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erotomania\" target=\"_blank\">erotomania</a> on the Path of Ecstasy. He was running a feeding scene and came on a pretty woman in a car with her daughter. He decided that the daughter was clearly coming on to him because she pushed her stuffed animal up to the window as he passed. He went up to the car pretending to be a window cleaner and then got incensed when he saw how pretty the woman was (Appearance 4). He Dominated the woman to get out of the car and put her child on the street, then in front of the child (still strapped into her car seat) proceeded to mutilate the mother with a knife. The child was crying of course as her mother is being savagely attacked. He then proceeded to rape the child on top of the bleeding wreck of the mother right there in the street.<br /> <br /> Then to top it all off, with the little girl crying and screaming he said that only babies cry, and that if she was going to be a baby she belonged back in her mother. He then proceeded to use Vicissitude to widen the mother's vagina and shove the child back in. Given the size of the child this killed the mother and child, ripping apart the mother and suffocating the child. He then left the body on the street and walked off whistling.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah\u2026I have sick friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:31:23-08:00","id":77715,"title":"","content":"Damn, that's hardcore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:08:18-08:00","id":80589,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Hermetics being assholes, my Mind Master's preferred tactic for dealing with Vampires in his city was to poison their dreams and screw with willpower recovery until they couldn't resist an implanted suggestion that they kill themselves. He did what he could to encourage them to end themselves messily and <i>publicly</i>, as an additional strike against the Technocratic Paradigm. Usually he'd apply this tactic to vampires he hadn't ever encountered personally. He'd just cast his spells out into the city hunting for minds with the right shape, and then scry on them for a while. If they seemed like the conscientious type who tried to avoid causing harm and being a burden, they didn't get a free pass, but they got put lower on the &quot;To Murder&quot; list (with the explicit objective of wiping them <i>all</i> out eventually). But if they were a Tremere, regardless of the characteristics of the individual, he would <i>wreck their mind</i>, and prioritize them higher than even vicious mass-murderers of other clans and bloodlines.<br /> <br /> This eventually drew enough heat to get him assassinated. By a member of the Inner Circle. But the important thing is that nobody, <i>nobody</i> in that campaign setting had any further smack to talk about House Merinita's &quot;<i>sissy faerie dream magicks</i>&quot; any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T23:41:03-08:00","id":81963,"title":"","content":"For my very first <i>Vampire</i> character, I crossed-out Empathy and replaced it with Apathy.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I was a trench-coat wearing, Skinny Puppy listening goth-punk kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T11:19:26-08:00","id":86133,"title":"","content":"Well... where to start.<br /> <br /> In my end of the world campaign in the early 90's the characters had already aligned, according to a prophesy, with the Wyrm being comprised of a newly awakened Mage a kin to BSD's, a Lost Cub and a Fomor, all started as normal humans, with a single human left standing they had to participate to a holy communion to show their devotion to the Holy Divinity of the Wyrm which was held in an old Church where the Priest sacrifised a human baby to make the communion &quot;wine&quot; and &quot;wafer&quot;. Earlier in the same game the Mage had already sacrificed one player to summon a Maeljin Incarna to aid them so just one more step on the path of Destruction.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite Changeling NPC's is a Bogie named Marrow whose dining habits concerning humans should be obvious.<br /> <br /> In a Sabbat game I had an Toreador Antitribu character who created his art of pain from human victims. His great masterwork being four pillars formed of preserved and sown together corpses made in the honor of the new Archbishop. Since he is a Toreador he lacks Vicissitude and so is limited to more mundane methods of creating his art through careful cuts, stitches and placement of human organs and parts.<br /> <br /> Also my otherwise quite cheerful Devil Tiger, originally a Dhampyr, once carefully peeled the skin of his victim while salting his flesh and yes the victim in that occurrence was a supernatural being that to his ill fortune couldn't escape the pain through dying.<br /> <br /> These are just from the top of my head and I'm sure are actually pretty far from the Darkest/grimiest thing I would have done or ST'd.<br /> <br /> Oh in my last VtM game a Tremere researcher NPC managed to alchemically turn all the vitae within a test subject vampire into a solid material that one of the PC's had the displeasure of cutting out of the test subject collecting it for the next part of the experiment. Naturally the test subject did not survive and the whole experience was rather harrowing to the poor PC trying to cling to his humanity amidst all this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:06:15-08:00","id":86729,"title":"","content":"Im pretty sure every Classic WoD answer should be wraith, and should have to do with something awful one by the shadow. As far as the grossest thing We ever did, a Tzimisce got a hold of a risen...and lets just say that was one monstrous ugly creature...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T18:37:53-07:00","id":89869,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Reckoning chronicle. Player was playing a punky-goth-computer nerd (Martyr Creed) with &quot;GET OFF MY BACK MOM&quot; parents (who actually loved him a whole lot, it was great).<br /> <br /> Antagonist: a Baali who was summoning up a demon. He had a Giovanni he hired out for zombies (write it off as &quot;labor outsourcing&quot; on your taxes), and a Tzimisce who was ancient, but also in Torpor, so he basically used the &quot;guy's&quot; Viscissitude by whispering into his ears and then the tendrils did the rest (yes, &quot;guy.&quot; Look, this Tzimisce was really more of a &quot;thing;&quot; when it finally woke up and became the primary antagonist, two and a half chronicles later, one of the players who could discern names asked what it's was and the response was &quot;The Skin Hanging From the Mountain.&quot; Thing was old).<br /> <br /> Baali kidnaps the PCs parents, sleepy-talks the Tzimisce into sewing them onto the wall (made from living skin, of course) he made in the basement of a creepy house in the middle of nowhere, and then watched. Baali's plan: &quot;if the Martyr kills his parents, he gets a free pass, is probably useful for my goals, and also, gets to take the bodies down and find out what happend to their backsides. If he doesn't kill them, I shoot him through the heart with green hellfire and make his friends fight a demon.&quot;<br /> <br /> The PC ended up taking the hellfire to the heart. Note this means that his parents lived, and got to suffer on the wall as the place fell down around them. Another PC died dragging the Baali into the gate (In a very Buffy-esque Hellmouth sequence, might I add). Good chronicle. Lots of blood.<br /> <br /> The Prophecy the Baali was trying to fulfill involved stuffing demonic spirits into kids, then feeding said kids the people who loved them most? That may also rank on the list of &quot;grim things I've done.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if this was a thread about hillarity, it would definitely be &quot;the Wraith game where the first thing the PCs do with the Relic car they stole is accidentally run over a ferryman.&quot;<br /> Botches are great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 03-12-2014, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T22:49:29-07:00","id":91411,"title":"","content":"In our long running Dark Ages chronicle there have been various stretches of darker or grimier sessions which have included accidentally igniting a race war in Cordova, accidentally releasing a demon (also Cordova), watching Baghdad burn under mongol assault, being unable to stop the black death, one member of our party unleashing several earthquakes on Jerusalem by accident and dint of scientific method. However, the most recent arc has probably taken the cake for the small group of sessions which we've referred as 'The Trough'.<br /> <br /> It was Florence in 1387 with the first embers of the Anarch revolt stirring in the city beneath the guise of the Ciompi uprising. The Setite member of our party had been tasked with retrieving relics of the faith within the city and following the trial of a suspected heretic/infernalist, her fellow Setites within the city have been labelled the most incompetent vampires we've met to date. They'd both been effectively abandoned and discarded by their sire and therefore had not been trained properly in the ways of Set or in being Cainites. These individuals were known as Cavolo di Pavia and Tomassino, who managed somehow to fail at running running a brothel due to Cavolo's love of spending all their money and Tomassino... just... just being himself. To emphasise exactly how terrible this den of inequity known as the 'Golden Orchid' was: they sold watered down vinegar instead of ale, provided and smoked hemp rope, employed a single elderly prostitute with no teeth who specialised in gumming, their altar was a poorly painted golden snake with a smily face, their priestess was aforementioned prostitute, their grasp of Set was mostly focused around hemp and sex. They each possessed minimal discipline knowledge, one was unaware he even possessed clan disciplines, neither knew what serpentis was, one didn't even know he could ghoul people.<br /> <br /> Cavolo was the oilyiest, slimeyiest, most incompetent bastard in the city (or so we thought) who it turned out had been rapidly embraced to be used as a footsoldier in Naples against the invading Tzimisce, he'd then chosen to abandon the Setite ways in favour of walking the road of Sin. Tomassino had been a strippling stable-boy (about 11-13) who had been embraced by his domitor out of pity ('a pity fuck embrace' our ST said) who then was abandoned due to being no-longer interesting, he was bullied by pretty much every vampire going. So pitiable was Tomassino that we discovered he'd attempted to take our Setites lessons to heart on a small gang of young noble-men who had been victimising and gang-raping him over the last few months, he'd accidentally convinced them to do the same to a large number of other young-men of lower birth in the city because they wouldn't be caught (an actual historical occurance). When our Setite heard this she decided to enact vengance and used Tomassino to lure the perpetrators out one by one, pin them down and make Tomassino take his revenge upon them in kind.<br /> Then we investigated Cavolo to discover that he was in the possession of the sorcerous books we searched for... but it seemed was also an infernalist despite having no knowledge of such, when he attempted to jump and stake our Setite my Tzimisce rendered him into torpor with a single kick to the testicles. We proceeded then to track down his haven (beneath another shitty tavern) which was guarded by his ghoul and discovered his tomes, where it turned out that a unknown benefactor had been handing him books which contained infernalist marginalia which summoned particular spirits / efreet to bargain with and would cause the individual to end up selling their soul to apep. We discovered also that Cavolo had been tainting some of the hempen rope with his small supply of opium, we also discovered the individual who was referred to as 'Pet'.<br /> 'Pet' had at one point six or seven years beforehand been a young noblewoman from the Frescobaldi family who had been slumming it amongst the seedier parts of the city, where Cavolo had attempted to seduce her into his twisted ways of Set (and the path of Sin). When she attempted to return home Cavolo had panicked and captured her, knowing that the vampire patriarch of the family would not take kindly to him poaching. He decided to ghoul her then and have a Cappadocian Sinner surgically remove her eyes, ears, nose, teeth alongside her arms and legs above the knees/elbows. She'd then been placed in a cage where she was fed blood and little food, subjected to repeated presence and used as a sexual slave while living in her own filth. His other ghoul routinely fed her his defications and glass when Cavolo wasn't paying attention. Needless to say she was put out of her misery, the other ghoul tortured to death by my character in a fit of rage, and the Prince of the city gave Cavolo a similar horrendous torturing before Cavolo was handed to our setite for merciful execution.<br /> <br /> There was a similarly unplesant and pig-headed individual known as Warden Du'Bois in a local town, who alongside his men was a serial rapist that almost ended up being fleshcrafted into a woman, embraced and handed over to the Fae (long story involving accidental murder of the Winter King's daughter) before our resident Brujah frenzied over the wardens foul-mouthed insulting despite the chances of redemption or death. The exact turn of phrase I believe was that the Brujah would be made the 'donky bitch', extrapolate from there, the warden luckily died horribly under the hands of the frenzying brujah.<br /> <br /> There was then the incident in which the malkavian elder known as Juliana Di Patsi after damning Cavolo by handing him tainted artefacts (for mocking her choice of hat and embarassing her two decades beforehand) and banishing the setites form the city with her favour from the prince, was murdered by our Setite during the revolution. She was forced to flee from assault by the elders twelve ghouled children bodyguards who proceeded before our eyes to tear and entire family apart in their own home. My Tzimisce and the Tremere bonded over the shared experience of trapping the children in that home and burning it down around them, as well as beating the escaped burning child to death with sticks while screaming in horror. This extended scene was made helarious/horrific by our STs extended mimicery of the childrens screams and shouts as they murdered/were burned to death.<br /> Florence has as such left something of a mark on our veteran PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:00:04-07:00","id":93410,"title":"","content":"Violence, gore, demon worshipping and such stuff are no strangers to my stories. But the really dark parts are always in the psychology. Like when I put one of the PC's in a V:tm chronicle, a Toreador following Path of Cathari, in a situation that taught her about how evil her character really was. She had to encourage a pedophile that were trying to better himself to continue his vile acts or risk loosing her path rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T20:28:13-07:00","id":94049,"title":"","content":"quick question, if Realdeadguy posts &quot;I made wraith the oblivion.&quot; Does he insta wins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T22:05:51-07:00","id":95409,"title":"","content":"Its either that or him and the next indivdual put forward their second best stories and we compare them.<br /> I agree dealing with IgynteZero on the fact that psychology is one of the most terrifying and harrowing things about world of Darkness, especially when you are walking Paths/Roads/Dharma, one of the most difficult things to deal with for a recent Werewolf the Apocalpyse campaign was balancing human morality with the requirements of being Garou. This is especially enjoyable/challenging with Children of Gaia in the group (in our case stoner lupus theurge and perfect family life ragabash).<br /> Several characters had trouble given their close connection to their kinfolk or their own personal experiences. My character for instance was a hungarian pretty-boy/playboy who hated the entire structure of his family and attempted to escape before he became a Garou, given the abuse he suffered in private schools and at home he leapt at the chance of recolonising a territory, but then had to balance his preconceptions with practicailties of Alphadom. Attempting to protect both of his sisters while trying to let them live their own lives, one of them ended up in a relationship with the eldest son of our 'scummy chav mommy' Bonegnawer Philodox (who was extremely family orientated due to being a runaway), the other became the ghoul of a vampire and we ended up starting a war with said vampires due to rescuing her. Amusingly my character and the bonegnawer ended up in a romantic relationship which somehow none of the rest of the pack managed to discover. Both characters met a sticky but not permanent end in the session before last when they faced down another pack over a abused kinfolk (my character couldn't let her run away and possibly get preyed upon elsewhere, but he couldn't give her back or give up one of their kinfolk in exchange. So, fight time.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","user":"Kale Fangblade","date":". 03-21-2014, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T23:13:23-07:00","id":96207,"title":"","content":"I played a Tzimisce that loved making warghouls for the prince and high rollers of the city. While that is not out of the ordinary for the clan, the method i used to gain a crafting bonus was a bit creative. I managed to obtain an elephant through an owed favor and after ghouling so it wouldn't die, reconfigured it into four walls a ceiling and a floor for an at home vicissitude bodyshop. after that at any given time i had about a dozen or so hobos worth spare parts hooked up to it all neatly sorted, left and right arms there, skins, torso/head combos and various organs all plugged into the elephant so they stayed alive and easier to manipulate. According to the group the worst was the three guys who had their skeletons fused together that i used as dressing mannequins since i loved tattoos but was indecisive on which ones to wear out on the town each day. Technically every one of them was alive and in varied levels of awake as i could need to build or repair a warghoul most any time(the town had a pesky wolf problem and they just got into everything).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2135,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2135-disodium-benzoate","user":"DIsodium Benzoate","date":". 03-22-2014, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2135-disodium-benzoate","name":"DIsodium Benzoate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T08:31:49-07:00","id":96349,"title":"","content":"As a PC, definitely some of the crap I pulled as my Tremere in TC.<br /> <br /> Story #1: Transylvanian Planned Parenthood<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It was during the third story in book 1, when the ritual to bind Kupala is being complete. The conspiracy got stuck in a town due to the weather, and couldn't move forward...my character who was a fledgling koldun (he'd spent a century hunting down and diablerizing Tzimisce to process and write down their memories of koldunic sorcery as they flooded him, in order to write an introductory treatise and start learning the discipline) knew it was Kupala behind it, and attempted an improvised ritual sacrifice to appease it. My character reasoned out virginal sacrifice might do the trick, but after rampaging through the town with auspex and dominate there were no virgin girls in the village (lots of girls though, so apparently we ran into PedoTown).<br /> <br /> So, I did the next best thing. Rounded up all the pregnant women in the village, cut the fetuses out and buried the fetuses alive, and let the pregnant women bleed out while the umbilical cord was still attached. We distracted the brujah PC who had a hatred of those who would harm children, by not-so-subtly letting it slip to him none of the young girls in the village were virgins and letting that run its natural course. Of course, my character fucked up the roll to actually perform the ritual, so my character basically murdered a bunch of pregnant women in an excessively cruel way while a pack of frenzied (or just bored) vampires slaughtered and burned an entire village for no reason whatsoever.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Story #2: Fuck You, Nova Arpad<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">When we finally got our hands on Nova Arpad later in the chronicle (i.e. the storyteller took the plot armor off), she tried to escape because she knew we were gunning for her in a big way and would rather greet the sun than let us have our way with her. <b>Tried</b> to escape.<br /> <br /> First, we cut out her eyes and replaced them with railroad spikes to keep her from regrowing them. Cut out her tongue and poured molten lead in her mouth and down her throat -- I did a ritual or two on her to make sure she could soak it. Denied the ability to use dominate or presence, we took turns taking turns hitting her with our nastiest and most fun curses and locking her in an Oubliette. Considering the conspiracy had between the PC's Thaumaturgy 8, Necromancy 8, Koldunic Sorcery 6, Obtenebration (and abyss mysticism) 8, Akhu 7, Wanga 6 or 7, and Dur-an-Ki 5 or 6...that took a while, and we didn't get bored for a <b>very</b> long time. After that, we took turns leaving her in just enough sunlight to incap and forced her to heal it back, impaled her and left her starving...you know, the boring stuff that got old fast.<br /> <br /> Then, the group's Setite performed Dismemberment of Osiris on her but &quot;forgot&quot; it only works on males. So, really we vivisected her for funsies. So, I used Biothaumaturgical Experimentation on her to give her a penis (and a bunch of other weirdo humiliating shit), so we could do Dismemberment again, and right that time. DoS doesn't necessarily kill vampires, and there's a fun little loophole that the soul doesn't actually have to be in the body at the time, so in the meantime I pulled her soul out with Necromancy and bound it. Her body got a parting gift, though...bane spirits!<br /> <br /> So, I forced her to watch her own mewling, rapidly-decaying, vivisected, possessed fomor body eat itself and die. Then I told just enough of her soul to the Baali for like $1.50 to ensure her eternal damnation after her spirit ended up freed, let me spectre slaves feed off her for a while (turns out when you've tormented and tortured somebody like Nova Arpad that much for that long, she's a real Pathos banquet), got bored eventually and had another spirit slave craft what was left of her spirit into a soulsteel anal plug, and just threw it out...in the Labyrinth.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm the only person that ST has ever explicitly banned from ever playing a clan, with no exceptions whatsoever. That would be Tzimisce, and because he's terrified of what I'd do with Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-22-2014, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}